# FV9-rulings.py · D3 pass 10, floor v9: R-21 (b)'s rulings file under R-26 and H10-2, written from this seat's reading
# of every line prose-sweep.mjs prints over floor v9 (FV9-records/sweep-fv9.log), each read with the whole sentence it
# belongs to and, where a clause names a mechanism, a value, a count or a line, against the floor v9 tree (and HEAD, to
# tell `reported` from false). Each ruling is `{ at, says, verdict, why }`; `says` is the printed line's own text, so a
# ruling goes stale the moment its line moves or changes.
#   verdict "true"      every clause of the line and of its sentence is true on floor v9; `why` names what makes each so
#                       (the file's reading below names each printed line by number where its clauses differ).
#   verdict "reported"  a clause is false, was false at HEAD (the line is byte-identical there), and the patch did not
#                       write it (R-26). Gates nothing; for the landing docs pass.
#   no ruling           a clause is false and the patch made it so. The line prints unread and the sweep FAILs: R-24's
#                       last sentence sends it to the critic, not into this build (FALSE below).
#   python3 -I FV9-rulings.py <sweep-fv9.log> <out.json>
